@startuml repository
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
title Repository: Reads, Caching, Writes and Error Boundaries

participant "Domain caller" as Domain
participant "SyncRepository actor" as Repo
participant "NSFileCoordinator" as Coordinator
database "Files / conflict versions" as File
collections "decodedFiles\nkey = symlink-resolved path" as Cache

== Read a domain's device records ==
Domain -> Repo : read(domain, type, connectionID)
Repo -> Repo : check connection generation and root availability
Repo -> Coordinator : coordinated listing of UUID directories in Devices
loop domain file and its unresolved conflict versions
  Repo -> Coordinator : coordinated readVersions
  Repo -> File : resourceValues (download status / identity / generation)
  alt file not downloaded yet
    Repo -> File : startDownloadingUbiquitousItem
    Repo --> Domain : SyncError.downloading
  else resource identity and generation both match, type matches
    Cache --> Repo : reuse the validated SyncRecord
  else no usable stamp, or stamp changed
    Repo -> File : read Data
    alt Data equals the cache and type matches
      Repo -> Cache : update stamp, reuse the decoded record
    else content changed or type differs
      Repo -> Repo : JSONDecoder + schema check
      Repo -> Cache : cache only successfully decoded content
    end
  end
  Repo -> Repo : check the record belongs to the device; remember conflict versions read
end
Repo --> Domain : records (the domain decides how to merge / pick the latest)
note over Repo,Domain
  Login: a single device's failure is logged and other devices continue.
  Playback / preferences: read failures are still thrown to the domain.
  A failed read removes the cache entry; failures are never cached.
end note

== Write this device's record ==
Domain -> Repo : write(record, domain / file)
Repo -> Repo : check connection (domain entry point)\nencode with JSONEncoder
Repo -> Coordinator : coordinated creation of the parent directory
Repo -> Coordinator : coordinated write of the target file
Repo -> Cache : invalidate the old entry
Repo -> File : Data.write(.atomic)
Repo -> File : query identity / generation
Repo -> Cache : store current Data, stamp and known record
loop only conflict versions observed by this domain's read
  Repo -> File : mark resolved and remove
  Repo -> Cache : drop the conflict's cache entry
end
Repo --> Domain : returns only when every step succeeded
note over Repo,File
  Current implementation: the resource query / conflict cleanup after the
  atomic write can still throw. This diagram does not claim that
  post-commit maintenance failures are handled separately.
  Filling the cache on success avoids re-decoding JSON for our own folder
  notifications; the notifications themselves still join request coalescing
  and are not filtered out by this device's ID.
end note

== Disconnect ==
Domain -> Repo : disconnect(old connectionID)
Repo -> Repo : only if it matches the current repository connection:\nrelease scopedURL / remove presenter\nclear folder, cache, conflicts and playback store state
@enduml
